@Transactional
public ComplaintResponse register(ComplaintRequest req) {
    if (req.evidenceId() == null || req.evidenceId().isBlank()) throw badRequest("缺少合成证据标识，不进入正式处置");
    LocalDateTime sampledAt = req.sampledAt().withOffsetSameInstant(ZoneOffset.UTC).toLocalDateTime();
    String fp = Fingerprints.of(req.stationCode(), req.frequencyMhz().toPlainString(), sampledAt.toString(), req.fieldStrengthDbuv().toPlainString(), req.evidenceId());
    // idempotent by requestId
    var existing = complaintRepo.findByRequestId(req.requestId());
    if (existing.isPresent()) {
        Complaint c = existing.get();
        if (!c.fingerprint().equals(fp)) throw conflict("同 requestId 参数不一致");
        return toResponse(c, true, false);
    }
    var natural = complaintRepo.findByNaturalKey(...);
    if (natural.isPresent()) return toResponse(natural.get(), false, true);
    long id;
    try {
        id = complaintRepo.insert(...);
    } catch (DuplicateKeyException e) {
        // 并发同键：重读裁决
        var again = complaintRepo.findByRequestId(req.requestId());
        if (again.isPresent()) {
            if (!again.get().fingerprint().equals(fp)) throw conflict(...);
            return toResponse(again.get(), true, false);
        }
        var nat = complaintRepo.findByNaturalKey(...);
        if (nat.isPresent()) return toResponse(nat.get(), false, true);
        throw e;
    }
    // 触发判定
    guardRepo.lock(freq);
    Long eventId = null;
    int stations = complaintRepo.countDistinctStations(freq, sampledAt.minusMinutes(30), sampledAt);
    if (stations >= 3 && !eventRepo.existsUnresolvedByFrequency(freq)) {
        var tx = transmitterRepo.findByFrequency(freq);
        if (tx.isPresent()) {
            eventId = eventRepo.insert(freq, tx.get().id(), id, now());
            complaintRepo.markTriggered(id, eventId);
        }
    }
    return new ComplaintResponse(id, false, false, eventId != null, eventId);
}
```

Wait: duplicate-key catch inside @Transactional — in Spring, if the SQL exception occurs, the transaction may be marked rollback-only? With DataSourceTransactionManager, the tx is not automatically marked rollback-only on exception (only if exception propagates through @Transactional boundary). Catching inside is fine; connection still usable. H2: after a constraint violation, the statement is rolled back, transaction continues. OK.

But subtle issue: concurrent same-requestId inserts — second tx's insert blocks until first commits (unique index), then throws DuplicateKeyException; re-read finds the committed row. Good.

For the trigger window: "同一频率在 30 分钟（UTC）内收到 3 个不同监测站的有效投诉" — window based on sampled_at of the new complaint. OK as designed.

